{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/914573-semiformed-conspiracy-idea-x-risk-control","id":914573,"title":"Semiformed conspiracy idea- X-Risk Control","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-14T19:19:27-07:00","id":914573,"title":"Semiformed conspiracy idea- X-Risk Control","content":"So this started out as an idea for a Compact or Conspiracy that fights mechanical or technomagical beings and mad scientists, and then turned into my porting an organization from some other writing (heavily eclipse phase-inspired) I've done into ChroD. I have no idea if this is workable and I have only the most basic outline, but I came up with an Endowment for them that I think is pretty neat. Their concept is that they deal with &quot;x-risks&quot;, risks that could theoretically endanger all of humanity, and their Endowment is essentially various gadgets designed to take on &quot;apocalyptic&quot; threats that have monster-fighting applications. <br /> <br /> Examples:<br /> <br /> Anti-nanobot &quot;blue goo&quot; that deals aggravated damage to swarms<br /> <br /> A gas that causes corpses (and other undead beings) to rapidly decay, designed to prevent a possible zombie apocalypse <br /> <br /> Again, it's not a very compete idea, but here's the germ of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T19:28:37-07:00","id":914578,"title":"","content":"As a huge Eclipse Phase nerd, this appeals to me. I like the idea that they're likely to turn a blind eye to powerful threats that don't meet their scale requirement; who cares if a vampire is feeding on the college kids in this one town when there are threats out there that can engulf continents? Maybe give them an origin within the CDC or FEMA, the type of organization who can view things on a properly macro scale. <br /> <br /> Zombies are probably their biggest target, but I'm sure parasites terrify them as well. Maybe they could be spun as a group targeting Hosts, from Werewolf?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-14T20:22:23-07:00","id":914608,"title":"","content":"Well, I kind of want to keep them focused to some degree on &quot;technological&quot; threats, because I feel like ChroD has been emphasizing the weird science angles lately and there's definitely a niche for a hunter group that deals with that.<br /> <br /> I'm not super sure how aware they would be of the Hosts- they're obviously X-Risks but I'm not sure how widespread awareness of them or of the existence of spirits in general actually is. Though there's definitely a niche for a Host-hunting group. There's one for a zombie hunter group, too. Actually, why not have a Compact or Conspiracy in the CDC based on dealing with supernatural diseases? I might actually write that up too, I really like that idea. My current tentative origin is that they emerged after WW2 as a coalition of Russian, American, and Chinese scientists, political thinkers, and military personnel, in response to the unprecedented danger of nuclear weaponry. <br /> <br /> And yeah, they'd totally be the type to do a lot of comprising. I actually think it would be interesting to see a hunter group that deals directly with other supernatural organizations without it being a Dark Secret the way it is with TFV, since this group's mission statement is such that it's probably SOP for members to work with lesser evils against greater ones. <br /> <br /> I'm toying with &quot;Protocols&quot; as the name for their endowment, maybe &quot;Endowment: X Protocols&quot;, with the X being a person of place important to the organization. Like, &quot;The Tunguska Protocols&quot; or something.<br /> <br /> About actual mechanics, I imagine the anti-zombie gas working on anything made from corpses- vampires, non-unfleshed Prometheans, maybe mummies. Though I think using the Blush of Life would protect against it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5358,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","user":"Geckopirateship","date":". 06-14-2016, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5358-geckopirateship","name":"Geckopirateship","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5358_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1383"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}